// REJECTS: Field 'data' is required
//
// The ExternalFormat embedded-data island requires BOTH contentType and data. Its grammar is
// `definition: (contentType | data)* EOF` -- each optional, each repeatable, in any order --
// so an island carrying only a content type is a complete parse of a useless payload.
//
// Islands are the place a rewrite is most likely to stop at "the delimiters matched", and
// this is what is enforced after they do.
###Data
Data fixture::neg::ExternalFormatWithoutData
{
   ExternalFormat
   #{
      contentType: 'application/json';
   }#
}
